r so it can  actually tell  um if the  if your back pressure suddenly spikes up  it's pretty sure that there's a blockage  in your nebulizer it will alert you of  that and you can set it up so that it  actually gives you  a pop-up  on your screen that says hey we think  your nebulizer's blocked  it will also  in the same vein as it's monitoring your  back pressure if that back pressure  crashes and there's just no back  pressure anymore then it assumes that  the nebulizers come on uh come  unconnected or something to that effect  and it will give you a pop-up message as  well so  rather than running  all day or all night with uh  with a nebulizer that's uh  that's crashed on you um and wasting all  that sample all those resources um  which is soul killing i know because  i've been there this will allow you to  stop it it'll stop your run and you can  go back and and take care of things  uh clean up your nebulizer replace the  nebulizer and start over what have you  stuff you wouldn't know until maybe you  uh  maybe you came in in the morning or  somebody else happened to look at or go  over and look at the data  this actually gives you a pop-up message  that indicates that there's a problem  so i think that's really cool  as  someone who's who's done this um  intelligent rinse is uh is something  that we added in this version of  software  um now this isn't something where  it rinses different times  it will only rinse a maximum amount in  this case it'll ask you what your max  rinse time is in we set it at 60 seconds  but that's the most it will ever rinse  but what it will do is monitor the lines  that you specify at the levels that you  specify and if  it returns to the same stable baseline  that it determined before the analysis  then it will stop rinsing  for instance if you're running brine  samples and it returns back to  the previously determined stable  baseline  for sodium  it will keep going um  and if it hasn't it will rinse the  maximum amount and then 